/-!
# The Gysin map of a family of equations cutting out a closed subscheme

Let `π : X ⟶ S` be a morphism of schemes, let `f₁, …, f_c ∈ Γ(X, 𝒪_X)`, and let
`i : Z ⟶ X` be the closed subscheme they cut out. This file discharges the hypothesis
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.FormKernelGeneratedByEquations` from exactly that: the kernel of
`Ω^p_{X/S} ⟶ i_*Ω^p_{Z/S}` is generated by the sections `∑ f_j ω'_j + ∑ ω''_j ∧ d f_j`, and so
the Gysin map of [Stacks, Tag 0G83] and its characterising formula hold with no hypothesis beyond
the one the source states.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Gysin.pullbackExactOneForm_eval`: the pulled-back differential `d f_j` of a global
  function, read in `⋀^1(i^*Ω_{X/S})`, is the comparison of [Stacks, Tag 01CI] applied to the
  pullback of the exact one-form `d f_j`.
* `Stacks.Gysin.unit_comp_pushforward_leftMul`: **the mathematical heart.** Left multiplication by
  `d f_j` inside `⋀(i^*Ω_{X/S})`, read through restriction to `Z`, is restriction to `Z`
  preceded by the left wedge with `d f_j` on `X`. This is the multiplicativity clause of
  [Stacks, Tag 01CI] read backwards.
* `Stacks.Gysin.equationsPresentation_f_eq`: the first map of the presentation of
  [Stacks, Tag 01CJ], split into one summand per equation.
* `Stacks.Gysin.kernel_ι_pushforward_comparison_comp_eq_zero`: the kernel of
  `i_*⋀^{k+1}(i^*Ω_{X/S}) ⟶ i_*Ω^{k+1}_{Z/S}` is killed by any morphism killing the direct image
  of that first map.
* `Stacks.Gysin.isIso_formsComparison_of_eq_zero`: in degree zero the comparison
  `⋀^0(i^*Ω_{X/S}) ⟶ Ω^0_{Z/S}` is an isomorphism, both sides being the structure sheaf.
* `Stacks.Gysin.kernel_ι_formsComparison_comp_eq_zero`: the two cases combined.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.formKernelGeneratedByEquations_of_isCutOutByEquations`:
  **the kernel description holds whenever the equations cut out the closed subscheme.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.gysinMap` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.formRestriction_comp_gysinMap`: **[Stacks, Tag 0G83], the Gysin
  map and its formula**, for the closed subscheme cut out by the equations.

## Route

Restriction of `p`-forms factors as
`Ω^p_{X/S} ⟶ i_*i^*Ω^p_{X/S} ⟶ i_*⋀^p(i^*Ω_{X/S}) ⟶ i_*Ω^p_{Z/S}`,
the first map the unit of `i^* ⊣ i_*`, the second the comparison of [Stacks, Tag 01CI] — an
isomorphism — and the third the comparison of [Stacks, Tag 01CJ]. A morphism `ψ` out of
`Ω^p_{X/S}` killing every `f_j ω'` factors through the unit, by
`Stacks.Gysin.exists_comp_unit_eq`; what remains is that the induced morphism out of
`i_*⋀^p(i^*Ω_{X/S})` kills the kernel of the third map.

For `p = k + 1` that kernel is described by [Stacks, Tag 01CJ] fed with the conormal sequence of
[Stacks, Tag 01UZ]: it is the image of
`(⊕_j 𝒪_Z) ⊗ ⋀^k(i^*Ω_{X/S}) ⟶ ⋀^{k+1}(i^*Ω_{X/S})`, `e ⊗ ω ↦ d(f_j)(e) ∧ ω`. That map's source
is a tensor product, so a morphism out of its direct image cannot be tested on sections; instead
it is split into one summand per equation by
`SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.generatorMul_eq_sum`, and each summand factors through left
multiplication by the single global section `d f_j` of `⋀^1(i^*Ω_{X/S})`. Left multiplication by
`d f_j`, read through restriction, *is* the left wedge with `d f_j` on `X`, which `ψ` kills by
hypothesis — on the right by assumption, hence on the left by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.formLeftWedgeHom_exactOneFormSection_comp_eq_zero`.

For `p = 0` there is no such presentation, and none is needed: both `⋀^0(i^*Ω_{X/S})` and
`Ω^0_{Z/S}` are the structure sheaf of `Z`, so the third map is an isomorphism and its kernel
vanishes.

The number `c` of equations is an arbitrary natural number, as in the source, which writes
`f₁, …, f_c ∈ Γ(X, 𝒪_X)` with no restriction on `c`. The degenerate case `c = 0` is not argued
separately anywhere: it is the instance at `c = 0` of the same two steps, every sum and product
over the equations being empty there. Crossing the unit is `Stacks.Gysin.exists_comp_unit_eq`,
whose hypothesis `∀ j, f_j ψ = 0` is vacuous and whose quotient `ℱ/(f₁, …, f_c)ℱ` is the
cokernel of a morphism out of an initial object; and the kernel of the comparison of
[Stacks, Tag 01CJ] is killed because the sum over the equations that
`Stacks.Gysin.equationsPresentation_f_eq` splits the presentation's first map into is empty.

## Implementation notes

The index type of the equations is doubled: the Gysin construction counts them by
`Fin c`, while `Stacks.ConormalSequenceRight.IsCutOutBy` and `SheafOfModules.free` want an
index in the universe of the schemes. `Stacks.Gysin.isCutOutByEquations_ulift` reindexes the
sectionwise hypothesis along `Equiv.ulift`, and every statement about the presentation is phrased
for the `ULift` family.

**Every composition step below is taken in term mode**, through the seven private reassociation
lemmas at the head of the file, rather than with `rw` or `simp`. The reason is the two spellings
of the category of modules on `Z`: `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules` is a `def`, so a composite
whose intermediate object is a homogeneous piece `(pullbackFormsAlgebra i π).piece m` — of type
`SheafOfModules (Stacks.RingedSpace.structureRingSheaf Z.toRingedSpace)` — is not type-correct at
the transparency at which `rw` builds its motive, although it is by `rfl`. The reassociation
lemmas are stated for an abstract category, where no such mismatch can arise, and the chains are
assembled with `Eq.trans` and `congrArg`. For the same reason `Epi` for the direct image is
supplied by hand at the `SheafOfModules.{u} (CategoryTheory.Sheaf.toRingCat …)` spelling in which
[Stacks, Tag 01CJ] is stated.

The general form of the Gysin map, which assumes the kernel description rather than deriving it,
remains `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.gysinMapOfFormKernel` and
`formRestriction_comp_gysinMapOfFormKernel`; it is what the projection formula of
[Stacks, Tag 0G8C] is stated against. The cohomological Gysin map of [Stacks, Tag 0G8A],
`Stacks.DeRham.CohomologicalGysin.equationGysinHodgeMap`, is built from the unconditional
`gysinMap` below and takes `IsCutOutByEquations` rather than the kernel description. The two
tagged declarations here are the unconditional ones.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0G83](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0G83)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CI)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CJ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01UZ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01UZ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08KS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08KS)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite TopologicalSpace
open AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom
open RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction (opensMap)
open Stacks.RingedSpace (pullbackUnit)

universe u

namespace Stacks.Gysin

/-! ### Reassociation in an abstract category -/

/-- A morphism killing the kernel of `g` kills every morphism composing to zero with `g`. -/
private theorem comp_eq_zero_of_kernel {C : Type*} [Category* C] [Limits.HasZeroMorphisms C]
    {A B D T : C} {g : B ⟶ D} [Limits.HasKernel g] (v : A ⟶ B) (hv : v ≫ g = 0) (Ψ : B ⟶ T)
    (hΨ : Limits.kernel.ι g ≫ Ψ = 0) : v ≫ Ψ = 0 := by
  rw [← Limits.kernel.lift_ι g v hv, Category.assoc, hΨ, comp_zero]

/-- Reassociation of a four-fold composite bracketed in the middle. -/
private theorem assoc₃ {C : Type*} [Category* C] {A B D E T : C} (κ : A ⟶ B) (a : B ⟶ D)
    (b : D ⟶ E) (Ψ : E ⟶ T) : (κ ≫ a ≫ b) ≫ Ψ = κ ≫ a ≫ b ≫ Ψ := by
  rw [Category.assoc, Category.assoc]

/-- Two consecutive images of a functor, in front of a morphism, compose inside the functor. -/
private theorem map_comp_assoc {C D : Type*} [Category* C] [Category* D] (F : C ⥤ D)
    {P Q R : C} {T : D} (a : P ⟶ Q) (b : Q ⟶ R) (Ψ : F.obj R ⟶ T) :
    F.map a ≫ F.map b ≫ Ψ = F.map (a ≫ b) ≫ Ψ := by
  rw [F.map_comp, Category.assoc]

/-- The same, with a morphism into the first image prepended. -/
private theorem comp_map_comp_map {C D : Type*} [Category* C] [Category* D] (F : C ⥤ D)
    {M T : D} {P Q R : C} (u : M ⟶ F.obj P) (a : P ⟶ Q) (b : Q ⟶ R) (x : F.obj R ⟶ T) :
    (u ≫ F.map a) ≫ F.map b ≫ x = (u ≫ F.map (a ≫ b)) ≫ x := by
  rw [F.map_comp]
  simp only [Category.assoc]

/-- The image of a three-fold composite vanishes against `Ψ` as soon as its last two factors
do. -/
private theorem map_comp₃_comp_eq_zero {C D : Type*} [Category* C] [Category* D]
    [Limits.HasZeroMorphisms C] [Limits.HasZeroMorphisms D] (F : C ⥤ D) {P Q R W : C} {T : D}
    (a : P ⟶ Q) (b : Q ⟶ R) (c : R ⟶ W) (Ψ : F.obj W ⟶ T)
    (h : F.map b ≫ F.map c ≫ Ψ = 0) : F.map (a ≫ b ≫ c) ≫ Ψ = 0 := by
  rw [F.map_comp, F.map_comp, Category.assoc, Category.assoc, h, comp_zero]

/-- Reassociation moving a middle bracket one factor to the right. -/
private theorem assoc_shuffle {C : Type*} [Category* C] {A B D E G T : C} (w : A ⟶ B)
    (u : B ⟶ D) (c : D ⟶ E) (e : E ⟶ G) (Ψ : G ⟶ T) :
    (w ≫ u ≫ c) ≫ e ≫ Ψ = w ≫ (u ≫ c ≫ e) ≫ Ψ := by
  simp only [Category.assoc]

/-- Reassociation unbracketing a three-fold middle factor. -/
private theorem assoc_shuffle₂ {C : Type*} [Category* C] {A B D E G T : C} (w : A ⟶ B)
    (q : B ⟶ D) (u : D ⟶ E) (c : E ⟶ G) (Ψ : G ⟶ T) :
    w ≫ (q ≫ u ≫ c) ≫ Ψ = w ≫ q ≫ u ≫ c ≫ Ψ := by
  simp only [Category.assoc]

variable {X Z S : Scheme.{u}} (i : Z ⟶ X) (π : X ⟶ S)

/-! ### The comparison of Stacks 01CI for the algebra of relative differential forms -/

/-- The comparison of [Stacks, Tag 01CI] between the pullback of `Ω^•_{X/S}` and the exterior
algebra of `i^*Ω_{X/S}`. -/
noncomputable abbrev formsPullbackIso :
    Stacks.PullbackExteriorAlgebra.ExteriorAlgebraPullbackIso i.toLRSHom.toShHom
      (relativeDifferentialFormsAlgebra π)
      (Scheme.Modules.exteriorGenerator (relativeDifferentials π))
      (pullbackFormsAlgebra i π) (pullbackFormsGenerator i π) :=
  Stacks.PullbackExteriorAlgebra.exteriorAlgebraPullbackIso i.toLRSHom.toShHom
    (relativeDifferentialFormsAlgebra π)
    (Scheme.Modules.exteriorGenerator (relativeDifferentials π))
    (pullbackFormsAlgebra i π) (pullbackFormsGenerator i π)
    (Scheme.Modules.isExteriorAlgebra_exteriorAlgebra _)
    (isExteriorAlgebra_pullbackFormsAlgebra i π)

/-- The degree-`m` component of the comparison of [Stacks, Tag 01CI]:
`i^*Ω^m_{X/S} ⟶ ⋀^m(i^*Ω_{X/S})`. -/
noncomputable abbrev formsPullbackComparison (m : ℤ) :
    (Scheme.Modules.pullback i).obj (relativeDifferentialForms π m) ⟶
      (pullbackFormsAlgebra i π).piece m :=
  ((formsPullbackIso i π).app m).hom

/-- The comparison of [Stacks, Tag 01CJ] on differential forms:
`⋀^m(i^*Ω_{X/S}) ⟶ Ω^m_{Z/S}`. -/
noncomputable abbrev formsComparison (m : ℤ) :
    (pullbackFormsAlgebra i π).piece m ⟶ relativeDifferentialForms (i ≫ π) m :=
  (Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentialFormsComparison i π (i ≫ π) (𝟙 S) (by simp)).app m

/-- **Restriction of `m`-forms to the closed subscheme, factored through the comparison of
[Stacks, Tag 01CI] and that of [Stacks, Tag 01CJ].** -/
theorem formRestriction_eq (m : ℤ) :
    formRestriction i π m =
      (Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction i).unit.app
          (relativeDifferentialForms π m) ≫
        (Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).map (formsPullbackComparison i π m) ≫
          (Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).map (formsComparison i π m) :=
  (congrArg
    (fun θ => (Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction i).unit.app
        (relativeDifferentialForms π m) ≫ (Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).map θ)
    (relativeDifferentialFormsMap_eq i π m)).trans
    (congrArg
      (fun θ => (Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction i).unit.app
          (relativeDifferentialForms π m) ≫ θ)
      ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).map_comp (formsPullbackComparison i π m)
        (formsComparison i π m)))

/-- The direct image of the comparison of [Stacks, Tag 01CI] is an isomorphism. -/
instance isIso_pushforward_formsPullbackComparison (m : ℤ) :
    IsIso ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).map (formsPullbackComparison i π m)) :=
  ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).mapIso ((formsPullbackIso i π).app m)).isIso_hom

/-- **Restriction to `i_*⋀^m(i^*Ω_{X/S})` is an epimorphism**: the unit of `i^* ⊣ i_*` is one
along a closed immersion, by [Stacks, Tag 08KS], and the comparison of [Stacks, Tag 01CI] is an
isomorphism. -/
instance epi_unit_comp_pushforward_formsPullbackComparison [IsClosedImmersion i] (m : ℤ) :
    Epi ((Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction i).unit.app
        (relativeDifferentialForms π m) ≫
      (Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).map (formsPullbackComparison i π m)) :=
  haveI := Stacks.ClosedImmersion.epi_unit_app i (relativeDifferentialForms π m)
  inferInstance

/-- Restriction to `i_*⋀^•(i^*Ω_{X/S})` commutes with a transport of the degree. -/
theorem unit_comp_pushforward_formsPullbackComparison_eqToHom {d d' : ℤ} (hd : d = d') :
    (Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction i).unit.app
          (relativeDifferentialForms π d) ≫
        (Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).map (formsPullbackComparison i π d) ≫
          (Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).map
            (eqToHom (congrArg (pullbackFormsAlgebra i π).piece hd)) =
      eqToHom (congrArg (relativeDifferentialForms π) hd) ≫
        (Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction i).unit.app
            (relativeDifferentialForms π d') ≫
          (Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).map (formsPullbackComparison i π d') := by
  subst hd
  have h0 : (Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).map
        (eqToHom (congrArg (pullbackFormsAlgebra i π).piece (rfl : d = d))) = 𝟙 _ :=
    (Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).map_id _
  refine Eq.trans (congrArg
    (fun θ => (Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction i).unit.app
        (relativeDifferentialForms π d) ≫
      (Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).map (formsPullbackComparison i π d) ≫ θ) h0) ?_
  refine Eq.trans (congrArg
    (fun θ => (Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction i).unit.app
      (relativeDifferentialForms π d) ≫ θ) (Category.comp_id _)) ?_
  exact (Category.id_comp _).symm

/-! ### Degree zero -/

/-- **In degree zero the comparison of [Stacks, Tag 01CJ] on differential forms is an
isomorphism.** Both `⋀^0(i^*Ω_{X/S})` and `Ω^0_{Z/S}` are the structure sheaf of `Z`, and a
unital homomorphism of graded algebras whose degree-zero pieces are both the unit sheaf is
invertible there. -/
theorem isIso_formsComparison_of_eq_zero {m : ℤ} (hm : m = 0) :
    IsIso (formsComparison i π m) := by
  subst hm
  exact SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.isIso_unitalHom_app_zero
    (SheafOfModules.algebras _ (pulledBackDifferentials i π)).exteriorPieceZeroIsoUnit
    (SheafOfModules.algebras _ (pulledBackDifferentials i π)).exteriorPieceZeroIsoUnit_one
    (SheafOfModules.algebras _ (relativeDifferentials (i ≫ π))).exteriorPieceZeroIsoUnit
    (SheafOfModules.algebras _ (relativeDifferentials (i ≫ π))).exteriorPieceZeroIsoUnit_one _

/-! ### The pulled-back differential of an equation -/

/-- The pulled-back differential `d f_j` of a global function, read in `⋀^1(i^*Ω_{X/S})`. -/
noncomputable abbrev pullbackExactOneForm (b : Γ(X, ⊤)) :
    ((pullbackFormsAlgebra i π).piece 1).sections :=
  SheafOfModules.sectionsMap (pullbackFormsGenerator i π)
    (Stacks.ConormalSequenceRight.pulledBackDifferential i π b)

/-- **The pulled-back differential of a global function is the comparison of
[Stacks, Tag 01CI] applied to the pullback of its exact one-form.** -/
theorem pullbackExactOneForm_eval (b : Γ(X, ⊤)) (U : X.Opensᵒᵖ) :
    (pullbackExactOneForm i π b).eval ((opensMap i.toLRSHom.toShHom).op.obj U) =
      (formsPullbackComparison i π 1).val.app ((opensMap i.toLRSHom.toShHom).op.obj U)
        (pullbackUnit i.toLRSHom.toShHom (relativeDifferentialForms π 1) U
          ((exactOneFormSection π b).eval U)) := by
  have hres : (Stacks.ConormalSequenceRight.pulledBackDifferential i π b).eval
        ((opensMap i.toLRSHom.toShHom).op.obj U) =
      pullbackUnit i.toLRSHom.toShHom (relativeDifferentials π) U
        ((Scheme.Hom.universalRelativeDerivation π).d
          (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top : U.unop ≤ ⊤)).op b)) := by
    refine Eq.trans ((pulledBackDifferentials i π).val.congr_map_apply
      (Subsingleton.elim _ ((opensMap i.toLRSHom.toShHom).op.map
        (homOfLE (le_top : U.unop ≤ ⊤)).op)) _) ?_
    refine Eq.trans (Stacks.RingedSpace.pullbackUnit_restrict i.toLRSHom.toShHom
      (relativeDifferentials π) (homOfLE (le_top : U.unop ≤ ⊤)).op _) ?_
    exact congrArg (pullbackUnit i.toLRSHom.toShHom (relativeDifferentials π) U)
      ((Scheme.Hom.universalRelativeDerivation π).d_map
        (homOfLE (le_top : U.unop ≤ ⊤)).op b).symm
  refine Eq.trans (congrArg ((pullbackFormsGenerator i π).val.app
    ((opensMap i.toLRSHom.toShHom).op.obj U)) hres) ?_
  exact ((formsPullbackIso i π).map_generator U
    ((Scheme.Hom.universalRelativeDerivation π).d
      (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top : U.unop ≤ ⊤)).op b))).symm

/-- **Left multiplication by the pulled-back differential of an equation, read through
restriction to the closed subscheme, is the left wedge with the exact one-form on `X`.** This is
the multiplicativity clause of the comparison of [Stacks, Tag 01CI] read backwards, in the
degrees `(1, k)`; it is the one place where the exterior algebra of the pullback is compared with
the pullback of the exterior algebra. -/
theorem unit_comp_pushforward_leftMul (b : Γ(X, ⊤)) (k : ℤ) :
    (Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction i).unit.app
          (relativeDifferentialForms π k) ≫
        (Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).map (formsPullbackComparison i π k ≫
          (pullbackFormsAlgebra i π).leftMul 1 k (pullbackExactOneForm i π b)) =
      formLeftWedgeHom π (exactOneFormSection π b) k ≫
        (Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction i).unit.app
            (relativeDifferentialForms π (1 + k)) ≫
          (Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).map (formsPullbackComparison i π (1 + k)) := by
  refine SheafOfModules.hom_ext (PresheafOfModules.hom_ext fun U =>
    ModuleCat.hom_ext (LinearMap.ext fun ω => ?_))
  refine Eq.trans ?_
    ((formsPullbackIso i π).map_mul 1 k U ((exactOneFormSection π b).eval U) ω).symm
  exact congrArg
    (fun z => ((pullbackFormsAlgebra i π).mul 1 k).app
      ((opensMap i.toLRSHom.toShHom).op.obj U) z
      ((formsPullbackComparison i π k).val.app ((opensMap i.toLRSHom.toShHom).op.obj U)
        (pullbackUnit i.toLRSHom.toShHom (relativeDifferentialForms π k) U ω)))
    (pullbackExactOneForm_eval i π b U)

/-- **A morphism out of `i_*i^*Ω^m_{X/S}` is one out of `i_*⋀^m(i^*Ω_{X/S})`**, the comparison of
[Stacks, Tag 01CI] being an isomorphism. -/
theorem exists_comp_formsPullbackComparison_eq (m : ℤ) {T : X.Modules}
    (ψ' : (Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).obj
        ((Scheme.Modules.pullback i).obj (relativeDifferentialForms π m)) ⟶ T) :
    ∃ Ψ : (Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).obj ((pullbackFormsAlgebra i π).piece m) ⟶ T,
      (Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).map (formsPullbackComparison i π m) ≫ Ψ = ψ' :=
  ⟨inv ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).map (formsPullbackComparison i π m)) ≫ ψ',
    IsIso.hom_inv_id_assoc _ _⟩

/-- **The kernel of restriction of `m`-forms is killed by a morphism that factors through the
restriction to `i_*⋀^m(i^*Ω_{X/S})` and kills the kernel of the comparison of
[Stacks, Tag 01CJ].** The kernel of restriction, followed by restriction to
`i_*⋀^m(i^*Ω_{X/S})`, lands in that kernel. -/
theorem kernel_ι_formRestriction_comp_eq_zero (m : ℤ) {T : X.Modules}
    (Ψ : (Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).obj ((pullbackFormsAlgebra i π).piece m) ⟶ T)
    {ψ : relativeDifferentialForms π m ⟶ T}
    (hψeq : (Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction i).unit.app
          (relativeDifferentialForms π m) ≫
        (Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).map (formsPullbackComparison i π m) ≫ Ψ = ψ)
    (hkey : Limits.kernel.ι ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).map (formsComparison i π m)) ≫
      Ψ = 0) :
    Limits.kernel.ι (formRestriction i π m) ≫ ψ = 0 := by
  have hv : (Limits.kernel.ι (formRestriction i π m) ≫
        (Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction i).unit.app
            (relativeDifferentialForms π m) ≫
          (Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).map (formsPullbackComparison i π m)) ≫
      (Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).map (formsComparison i π m) = 0 :=
    (assoc₃ _ _ _ _).trans
      ((congrArg (fun θ => Limits.kernel.ι (formRestriction i π m) ≫ θ)
        (formRestriction_eq i π m).symm).trans (Limits.kernel.condition _))
  refine Eq.trans (congrArg
    (fun θ => Limits.kernel.ι (formRestriction i π m) ≫ θ) hψeq.symm) ?_
  exact (assoc₃ _ _ _ Ψ).symm.trans (comp_eq_zero_of_kernel _ hv Ψ hkey)

/-! ### Reindexing the equations into the universe of the schemes -/

/-- **The sectionwise condition that the equations cut out the closed subscheme is stable under
reindexing along `ULift`.** -/
theorem isCutOutByEquations_ulift {I : Type*} [Fintype I] {f : I → Γ(X, ⊤)}
    (hcut : IsCutOutByEquations i f) :
    IsCutOutByEquations i (fun j : ULift.{u} I => f j.down) where
  appTop_eq_zero j := hcut.appTop_eq_zero j.down
  exists_eq_sum U a ha x hx := by
    obtain ⟨V, hVU, hxV, c, hc⟩ := hcut.exists_eq_sum U a ha x hx
    exact ⟨V, hVU, hxV, fun j => c j.down,
      hc.trans (Fintype.sum_equiv (Equiv.ulift (α := I)) _ _ fun _ => rfl).symm⟩

/-- **The empty family of equations cuts out `X` itself.** Read at an empty index type, the
hypothesis `IsCutOutByEquations i f` of [Stacks, Tag 0G83] says that a function vanishing on `Z`
is locally the empty sum, that is, zero; so it asks exactly that `i` have vanishing ideal sheaf,
which is the source's `Z = X` in the case `c = 0`. The identity closed immersion satisfies it,
which is what this records: the `c = 0` case of `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.gysinMap` — and so
of `Stacks.DeRham.CohomologicalGysin.equationGysinHodgeMap`, the construction of
[Stacks, Tag 0G8A] — has a model and is not vacuous. -/
theorem isCutOutByEquations_id_of_isEmpty {I : Type*} [Fintype I] [IsEmpty I]
    (f : I → Γ(X, ⊤)) : IsCutOutByEquations (𝟙 X) f where
  appTop_eq_zero j := isEmptyElim j
  exists_eq_sum U a ha x hx := by
    refine ⟨U, le_rfl, hx, isEmptyElim, ?_⟩
    have h0 : a = 0 := ha
    rw [Finset.univ_eq_empty, Finset.sum_empty, h0, map_zero]

/-! ### The kernel of the comparison of Stacks 01CJ after direct image -/

variable {c : ℕ} {fu : ULift.{u} (Fin c) → Γ(X, ⊤)}

/-- **The first map of the presentation of [Stacks, Tag 01CJ], split into one summand per
equation.** Its `j`-th summand contracts the `j`-th coordinate of `⊕_j 𝒪_Z` and then multiplies
on the left by the pulled-back differential `d f_j`. -/
theorem equationsPresentation_f_eq
    (hf : Stacks.ConormalSequenceRight.IsCutOutBy i fu) (k : ℕ)
    (hk : (1 : ℤ) + (k : ℤ) = ((k + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ)) :
    (equationsPresentation i π hf k).f =
      (∑ j : ULift.{u} (Fin c),
        Stacks.SheafOfModules.freeCoordTensorHom
            ((pullbackFormsAlgebra i π).piece (k : ℤ)) j ≫
          (pullbackFormsAlgebra i π).leftMul 1 (k : ℤ) (pullbackExactOneForm i π (fu j)) ≫
            eqToHom (congrArg (pullbackFormsAlgebra i π).piece hk) :
        (equationsPresentation i π hf k).X₁ ⟶ (equationsPresentation i π hf k).X₂) := by
  classical
  have hγ : ∀ j : ULift.{u} (Fin c),
      ((pullbackFormsAlgebra i π).piece 1).freeHomEquiv
          (Stacks.ConormalSequenceRight.equationDifferentialsMap i π fu ≫
            pullbackFormsGenerator i π) j =
        pullbackExactOneForm i π (fu j) := by
    intro j
    refine Eq.trans (Stacks.ConormalSequenceRight.freeModulesHomEquiv_comp Z _
      (Stacks.ConormalSequenceRight.equationDifferentialsMap i π fu)
      (pullbackFormsGenerator i π) j) ?_
    exact congrArg (SheafOfModules.sectionsMap (pullbackFormsGenerator i π))
      (congrFun ((Stacks.ConormalSequenceRight.freeModulesHomEquiv Z _ _).apply_symm_apply _) j)
  refine Eq.trans (congrArg
    (fun θ => θ ≫ eqToHom (congrArg (pullbackFormsAlgebra i π).piece hk))
    (SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.generatorMul_eq_sum (I := ULift.{u} (Fin c))
      (Osharp := Z.sheaf) (Stacks.ConormalSequenceRight.equationDifferentialsMap i π fu)
      (pullbackFormsGenerator i π) (k : ℤ))) ?_
  refine Eq.trans (Preadditive.sum_comp _ _ _) ?_
  exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j _ =>
    (Category.assoc _ _ _).trans (congrArg
      (fun t => Stacks.SheafOfModules.freeCoordTensorHom
          ((pullbackFormsAlgebra i π).piece (k : ℤ)) j ≫
        (pullbackFormsAlgebra i π).leftMul 1 (k : ℤ) t ≫
          eqToHom (congrArg (pullbackFormsAlgebra i π).piece hk)) (hγ j))

/-- **A morphism out of `i_*⋀^{k+1}(i^*Ω_{X/S})` killing the direct image of the first map of
the presentation of [Stacks, Tag 01CJ] kills the kernel of the direct image of its second
map.** The presentation is exact at the middle term, so the first map factors through the kernel
by an epimorphism; direct image along a closed immersion preserves epimorphisms, by
[Stacks, Tag 08KS], and it preserves kernels, being a right adjoint. -/
theorem kernel_ι_pushforward_comparison_comp_eq_zero [IsClosedImmersion i]
    (hf : Stacks.ConormalSequenceRight.IsCutOutBy i fu) (k : ℕ) {T : X.Modules}
    (Ψ : (Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).obj
        ((pullbackFormsAlgebra i π).piece ((k + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ)) ⟶ T)
    (hz : (Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).map (equationsPresentation i π hf k).f ≫ Ψ = 0) :
    Limits.kernel.ι ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).map
        (formsComparison i π ((k + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ))) ≫ Ψ = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨hex, -⟩ := equationsPresentation_exact i π hf k
  have hlift : Epi (C := Z.Modules) (Limits.kernel.lift (equationsPresentation i π hf k).g
      (equationsPresentation i π hf k).f (equationsPresentation i π hf k).zero) :=
    hex.epi_kernelLift
  have hpe :=
    Stacks.ClosedImmersion.preservesEpimorphisms_modulePushforward_of_isClosedImmersion i
  have : Epi ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).map (Limits.kernel.lift
      (equationsPresentation i π hf k).g (equationsPresentation i π hf k).f
      (equationsPresentation i π hf k).zero)) :=
    @Functor.PreservesEpimorphisms.preserves _ _ _ _ _ hpe _ _ _ hlift
  have h1 : (Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).map
      (Limits.kernel.ι (C := Z.Modules) (equationsPresentation i π hf k).g) ≫ Ψ = 0 :=
    zero_of_epi_comp ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).map (Limits.kernel.lift
        (equationsPresentation i π hf k).g (equationsPresentation i π hf k).f
        (equationsPresentation i π hf k).zero))
      ((map_comp_assoc (Scheme.Modules.pushforward i) _ _ Ψ).trans
        ((congrArg (fun θ => (Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).map θ ≫ Ψ)
          (Limits.kernel.lift_ι _ _ _)).trans hz))
  refine Eq.trans (congrArg (fun θ => θ ≫ Ψ) (Limits.PreservesKernel.iso_inv_ι
    (Scheme.Modules.pushforward i) (equationsPresentation i π hf k).g).symm) ?_
  exact (Category.assoc _ _ Ψ).trans
    ((congrArg (fun θ => (Limits.PreservesKernel.iso (Scheme.Modules.pushforward i)
      (equationsPresentation i π hf k).g).inv ≫ θ) h1).trans comp_zero)

/-- **The kernel of `i_*⋀^p(i^*Ω_{X/S}) ⟶ i_*Ω^p_{Z/S}` is killed by any morphism whose
composite with restriction kills the wedges with the differentials of the equations.** This is
the two cases of the route combined: for `p = k + 1` the presentation of [Stacks, Tag 01CJ],
and for `p = 0` the comparison being an isomorphism. -/
theorem kernel_ι_formsComparison_comp_eq_zero [IsClosedImmersion i]
    {f : Fin c → Γ(X, ⊤)} (hcut : IsCutOutByEquations i f) {m : ℤ}
    (hm : m = 0 ∨ ∃ k : ℕ, m = ((k + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ)) {T : X.Modules}
    (Ψ : (Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).obj ((pullbackFormsAlgebra i π).piece m) ⟶ T)
    (hwedge : ∀ (q : ℤ) (hq : q + 1 = m) (j : Fin c),
      exactFormWedgeHom π (f j) q ≫
        eqToHom (congrArg (relativeDifferentialForms π) hq) ≫
          ((Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction i).unit.app
              (relativeDifferentialForms π m) ≫
            (Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).map (formsPullbackComparison i π m) ≫ Ψ) = 0) :
    Limits.kernel.ι ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).map (formsComparison i π m)) ≫ Ψ = 0 := by
  classical
  rcases hm with hm | ⟨k, hm⟩ <;> subst hm
  · have hiso : IsIso (formsComparison i π 0) :=
      isIso_formsComparison_of_eq_zero i π (m := (0 : ℤ)) rfl
    have : IsIso ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).map (formsComparison i π 0)) :=
      ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).mapIso
        (@asIso _ _ _ _ (formsComparison i π 0) hiso)).isIso_hom
    have hz : Limits.kernel.ι ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).map
        (formsComparison i π 0)) = 0 :=
      zero_of_comp_mono ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).map (formsComparison i π 0))
        (Limits.kernel.condition _)
    exact (congrArg (fun θ => θ ≫ Ψ) hz).trans zero_comp
  · have hk : (1 : ℤ) + (k : ℤ) = ((k + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) := by push_cast; ring
    have hk₂ : (k : ℤ) + 1 = ((k + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) := by push_cast; ring
    have hfu : Stacks.ConormalSequenceRight.IsCutOutBy i
        (fun j : ULift.{u} (Fin c) => f j.down) :=
      isCutOutBy_of_isCutOutByEquations i (isCutOutByEquations_ulift i hcut)
    refine kernel_ι_pushforward_comparison_comp_eq_zero i π hfu k Ψ ?_
    refine Eq.trans (congrArg (fun θ => (Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).map θ ≫ Ψ)
      (equationsPresentation_f_eq i π hfu k hk)) ?_
    refine Eq.trans (congrArg (fun θ => θ ≫ Ψ)
      ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).map_sum
        (fun j : ULift.{u} (Fin c) =>
          Stacks.SheafOfModules.freeCoordTensorHom
              ((pullbackFormsAlgebra i π).piece (k : ℤ)) j ≫
            (pullbackFormsAlgebra i π).leftMul 1 (k : ℤ)
                (pullbackExactOneForm i π (f j.down)) ≫
              eqToHom (congrArg (pullbackFormsAlgebra i π).piece hk))
        Finset.univ)) ?_
    refine Eq.trans (Preadditive.sum_comp _ _ Ψ) ?_
    refine Finset.sum_eq_zero fun j _ => ?_
    refine map_comp₃_comp_eq_zero (Scheme.Modules.pushforward i) _ _ _ Ψ ?_
    refine zero_of_epi_comp
      ((Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction i).unit.app
          (relativeDifferentialForms π (k : ℤ)) ≫
        (Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).map (formsPullbackComparison i π (k : ℤ))) ?_
    refine Eq.trans (comp_map_comp_map (Scheme.Modules.pushforward i) _ _ _ _) ?_
    refine Eq.trans (congrArg (fun θ => θ ≫ (Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).map
        (eqToHom (congrArg (pullbackFormsAlgebra i π).piece hk)) ≫ Ψ)
      (unit_comp_pushforward_leftMul i π (f j.down) (k : ℤ))) ?_
    refine Eq.trans (assoc_shuffle _ _ _ _ Ψ) ?_
    refine Eq.trans (congrArg
      (fun θ => formLeftWedgeHom π (exactOneFormSection π (f j.down)) (k : ℤ) ≫ θ ≫ Ψ)
      (unit_comp_pushforward_formsPullbackComparison_eqToHom i π hk)) ?_
    refine Eq.trans (assoc_shuffle₂ _ _ _ _ Ψ) ?_
    exact formLeftWedgeHom_exactOneFormSection_comp_eq_zero π (f j.down) k hk hk₂ _
      (hwedge (k : ℤ) hk₂ j.down)

end Stacks.Gysin

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom

variable {X Z S : Scheme.{u}}

/-- **The kernel of restriction of `p`-forms is generated by the equations and their
differentials, whenever the equations cut out the closed subscheme.** This is the hypothesis
`FormKernelGeneratedByEquations` that the construction of [Stacks, Tag 0G83] appeals to,
discharged from the source's own hypothesis on `Z`.

The proof is the route described in the module documentation: factor restriction through the
unit of `i^* ⊣ i_*` and the comparison of [Stacks, Tag 01CI], use
`Stacks.Gysin.exists_comp_unit_eq` to pass the morphism across the unit, and then kill the
kernel of the comparison of [Stacks, Tag 01CJ] with
`Stacks.Gysin.kernel_ι_formsComparison_comp_eq_zero`. -/
theorem formKernelGeneratedByEquations_of_isCutOutByEquations (i : Z ⟶ X) [IsClosedImmersion i]
    (π : X ⟶ S) {c : ℕ} {f : Fin c → Γ(X, ⊤)}
    (hcut : Stacks.Gysin.IsCutOutByEquations i f) (p : ℕ) :
    FormKernelGeneratedByEquations i π f (p : ℤ) := by
  intro T ψ hsmul hwedge
  obtain ⟨ψ', hψ'⟩ :=
    Stacks.Gysin.exists_comp_unit_eq i hcut (relativeDifferentialForms π (p : ℤ)) ψ hsmul
  obtain ⟨Ψ, hΨ⟩ :=
    Stacks.Gysin.exists_comp_formsPullbackComparison_eq i π (p : ℤ) ψ'
  have hψeq : (Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction i).unit.app
        (relativeDifferentialForms π (p : ℤ)) ≫
      (Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).map
        (Stacks.Gysin.formsPullbackComparison i π (p : ℤ)) ≫ Ψ = ψ :=
    (congrArg
      (fun θ => (Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction i).unit.app
        (relativeDifferentialForms π (p : ℤ)) ≫ θ) hΨ).trans hψ'
  have hm : (p : ℤ) = 0 ∨ ∃ k : ℕ, (p : ℤ) = ((k + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) := by
    cases p with
    | zero => exact Or.inl (by simp)
    | succ k => exact Or.inr ⟨k, rfl⟩
  exact Stacks.Gysin.kernel_ι_formRestriction_comp_eq_zero i π (p : ℤ) Ψ hψeq
    (Stacks.Gysin.kernel_ι_formsComparison_comp_eq_zero i π hcut hm Ψ
      fun q hq j => (congrArg
        (fun θ => exactFormWedgeHom π (f j) q ≫
          eqToHom (congrArg (relativeDifferentialForms π) hq) ≫ θ) hψeq).trans (hwedge q hq j))

section FractionClass

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0G83: the Gysin map.** Let `π : X ⟶ S` be a morphism of schemes, let
`f₁, …, f_c ∈ Γ(X, 𝒪_X)`, and let `i : Z ⟶ X` be the closed subscheme they cut
out, that is, let the ideal sheaf of `i` be generated by `f₁, …, f_c`. The Gysin map

`γ^p_{f₁, …, f_c} : Ω^p_{Z/S} ⟶ ℋ^c_Z(Ω^{p+c}_{X/S})`

is the unique morphism whose value on the restriction `ω̃|_Z` of a local `p`-form `ω̃` on `X` is
`c_{f₁, …, f_c}(ω̃|_Z) ∧ d f₁ ∧ ⋯ ∧ d f_c`. Both sheaves are read on `X` through the direct image
along `i`, which is faithful; `ℋ^c_Z` is the local cohomology sheaf and `c_{f₁, …, f_c}` the
canonical map of [Stacks, Tag 0G7Q].

**The content is well-definedness**, that is, independence of the chosen lift `ω̃`: the map
`gysinFormulaHom` kills the kernel of restriction to `Z`, because a lift is determined up to
`∑ f_j ω'_j + ∑ ω''_j ∧ d f_j` — that is
`formKernelGeneratedByEquations_of_isCutOutByEquations`, where the hypothesis on `Z` enters —
and both kinds of term go to zero, the first by `smulHom_comp_gysinFormulaHom`, the second by
`exactFormWedgeHom_comp_gysinFormulaHom`. The map is then the descent of `gysinFormulaHom` along
the epimorphism `formRestriction`, taken constructively with
`CategoryTheory.Abelian.epiDesc`. -/
@[stacks 0G83 "the Gysin map γ^p_{f_1, …, f_c}, for the closed subscheme cut out by the \
equations: no hypothesis beyond the source's own, that the ideal sheaf of i is generated by \
f_1, …, f_c."]
def gysinMap (i : Z ⟶ X) [IsClosedImmersion i] (π : X ⟶ S) {c : ℕ}
    (f : Fin c → Γ(X, ⊤)) (p : ℕ)
    (hcut : Stacks.Gysin.IsCutOutByEquations i f) :
    (Scheme.Modules.pushforward i).obj (relativeDifferentialForms (i ≫ π) (p : ℤ)) ⟶
      pushforwardLocalCohomology f
        (relativeDifferentialForms π ((p : ℤ) + (c : ℤ))) :=
  gysinMapOfFormKernel i π f p
    (formKernelGeneratedByEquations_of_isCutOutByEquations i π hcut p)

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0G83: the formula for the Gysin map.** On the restriction `ω̃|_Z` of a
local `p`-form `ω̃` on `X`, the Gysin map takes the value
`c_{f₁, …, f_c}(ω̃|_Z) ∧ d f₁ ∧ ⋯ ∧ d f_c`. This is the equation of the source, and it determines
`gysinMap` because restriction to `Z` is an epimorphism. -/
@[stacks 0G83 "the formula γ^p(ω) = c_{f_1, …, f_c}(ω̃|_Z) ∧ d f_1 ∧ ⋯ ∧ d f_c, for the closed \
subscheme cut out by the equations, with no hypothesis beyond the source's own."]
theorem formRestriction_comp_gysinMap (i : Z ⟶ X) [IsClosedImmersion i]
    (π : X ⟶ S) {c : ℕ} (f : Fin c → Γ(X, ⊤)) (p : ℕ)
    (hcut : Stacks.Gysin.IsCutOutByEquations i f) :
    formRestriction i π (p : ℤ) ≫ gysinMap i π f p hcut = gysinFormulaHom π f (p : ℤ) :=
  formRestriction_comp_gysinMapOfFormKernel i π f p _

end FractionClass

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom

